# Veer Real Estate — Project Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router, Turbopack default), React 19.2
- Drizzle ORM + postgres.js driver → Supabase Postgres
- Supabase Storage for all media (images, floor plans)
- TanStack Query v5 for client-side data fetching
- Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-based config via @theme inline in globals.css)
- Zod for all validation
- lucide-react for icons (NO Font Awesome, NO react-icons)
- sonner for toast notifications
- Plus Jakarta Sans (headings) + Inter (body) via next/font/google

## Next.js 16 Specific (CRITICAL — do not use Next.js 15 patterns)
1. proxy.ts NOT middleware.ts. Export function named `proxy`, not `middleware`.
2. proxy.ts is THIN — routing only. NO auth verification, NO DB calls.
3. Auth guard lives in admin layout.tsx as Server Component calling verifySession().
4. All params and searchParams are async:
   `const { slug } = await props.params`
5. next/image: Do NOT use onLoadingComplete, lazyBoundary, lazyRoot props.
6. Node.js 20+ minimum.
7. Turbopack is default — do NOT add webpack config.

## Architecture Rules
1. Public pages = Server Components. No 'use client' on page.tsx files.
2. Interactive UI = small client component islands imported into server pages.
3. Admin pages = client components, all data via TanStack Query hooks.
4. Every API call from a component goes through a hook in hooks/queries/ or hooks/mutations/.
5. API routes validate input with Zod before any DB operation.
6. API routes return { data } on success, { error: string } on failure.

## Color System — VARIABLES ONLY
All colors use CSS custom properties defined in globals.css :root.
Never hardcode hex values in components. Always use Tailwind classes mapped to variables:
- bg-primary, text-primary (navy #1A1A2E)
- bg-accent, text-accent, bg-accent-light, bg-accent-dark (warm copper #D48458)
- bg-accent-subtle (copper at 10% opacity for icon backgrounds, light fills, and badges)
- bg-surface (warm off-white), bg-card (white)
- text-text, text-text-muted, text-text-light, text-text-inverse
- border-border, border-border-light
- bg-success/warning/error/info and their -light variants
- shadow-card, shadow-card-hover, shadow-elevated
- bg-whatsapp (official WhatsApp green — only allowed brand hex exception)
NEVER use "gold" in class names or color references. The accent is always "accent".
To change the entire theme, edit :root in globals.css. Nothing else changes.

## Typography
- Headings: font-heading (Plus Jakarta Sans), font-bold/semibold, tracking-tight
- Body: font-body (Inter), font-normal, leading-relaxed
- Max body text width: max-w-prose
- No ALL CAPS on headings. Only on xs badges with tracking-wider.

## Component Patterns
- Cards: rounded-2xl, shadow-card, hover:shadow-card-hover. No borders.
- Buttons primary: rounded-xl bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-light (white text on copper — copper is dark enough for contrast)
- Buttons secondary: rounded-xl border border-primary text-primary hover:bg-primary hover:text-text-inverse
- Inputs: rounded-lg border-border focus:ring-accent
- Section padding: py-16 md:py-24
- Content max-width: max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4
- Stats: flat horizontal numbers, text-accent, no circles/boxes
- Icon wrappers: bg-accent-subtle text-accent rounded-xl p-2

## Database
- Schema changes ONLY through Drizzle migrations.
- drizzle-kit generate → review SQL → drizzle-kit migrate. No push in prod.
- Use pgEnum for categorical fields. JSONB for arrays.
- All tables have created_at/updated_at with timezone.

## SEO
- Every public route exports generateMetadata() with unique title + description.
- JSON-LD structured data on every public page (via `JsonLdScript` in `src/lib/seo.tsx`).
- Canonical site URL from `getSiteUrl()` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` in `src/lib/site.ts`.
- Public contact/office/social content lives in `src/lib/site.ts` — do not hardcode across pages.
- Semantic HTML: article, section, nav, address, time.
- /llms.txt and /llms-full.txt API routes for AI discoverability.
- Dynamic sitemap.ts and robots.ts.

## TanStack Query
- Centralized key factory in hooks/keys.ts.
- Mutations invalidate relevant keys via onSuccess.
- staleTime: 5min (public), 0 (admin).
- No raw fetch() in components.

## Media / Supabase Storage
- Uploads → /api/media/upload → Supabase Storage via `getSupabaseAdmin()` / `uploadToStorage()` in `src/lib/supabase.ts`. Never direct client upload.
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (Secret key `sb_secret_...` or legacy service_role JWT), `SUPABASE_BUCKET_NAME`.
- Do NOT use Publishable / anon key for uploads. Server uploads only with the Secret key.
- Storage bucket must be **public** so URLs work as `/storage/v1/object/public/{bucket}/{path}`.
- Public URL helper: `getPublicStorageUrl(path)` — uses `SUPABASE_BUCKET_NAME` from env.
- Keep storage paths organized, e.g. `projects/{slug}/cover.{ext}`, `projects/{slug}/gallery/{n}.{ext}`, `projects/{slug}/floor-plans/{n}.{ext}`, `blog/{slug}/cover.{ext}`, `blog/{slug}/og.{ext}`.
- Videos = YouTube embed URLs. No video file uploads.
- Images via Next.js <Image> with sizes attribute. Allow `**.supabase.co` in next.config remotePatterns.

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict. No `any` except migration scripts.
- Named exports for components. Default exports only for page.tsx.
- No console.log in production code.
